# Overview
#
# A fancy word stands in for a plainer one. `utilize` and `leverage`
# stand in for `use` (`leverage the cache`). The fancy word adds length
# and no meaning, and a reader who does not know it must look it up. The
# fix writes `use`, and the message names that plain word. The rule sits
# at Required, because both words have the same plain word and the
# pattern keeps to the verb `leverage`.
#
# Expression
#
# `$utilize` and `$utilise` expand to every form of the word through
# Harper's dictionary. They never misfire, so every form stays.
#
# `leverage` counts only as a verb with an object (`leverage the cache`,
# `leveraged its position`). The branch takes `leverage`, `leverages`,
# `leveraged`, or `leveraging` before a word that opens an object.
# Harper's part-of-speech tagger marks such a word with one of the tags
# in the branch. `DET` is a determiner, a word that introduces a noun,
# such as `the`, `a`, or `this`. `PRON` is a pronoun, and `ADJ` is an
# adjective. `PROPN` is a proper noun, a name that takes a capital
# letter, such as `Kubernetes`.
#
# The rule flags instead of replacing, because the match includes the
# object, which a rewrite to `use` drops.
#
# False Positives
#
# The noun `leverage` passes, because the noun is the common sense in
# finance, hardware, and negotiation prose (`leverage ratio`, `a
# leveraged buyout`, `more leverage`, `the leverage parameter`).
#
# Related Rules
#
# The Required ProseFancyWord holds `utilize` and `leverage`, whose
# plain word is always `use`. The Recommended ProseFancyWord holds the
# words that turn up far more in generated text than in docs a person
# wrote. Their plain word differs from word to word. The Optional
# ProseFancyWord holds the words that human-written docs also use.
#
# Measurement
#
# The rule hit 62 lines in the measure.py corpus, and in 20 of 20
# sampled hits `use` said the same. Of the 20, 17 were a form of
# `utilize` and 3 were the verb `leverage`.
expr main [$utilize, $utilise, ([leverage, leverages, leveraged, leveraging] [DET, PRON, PROPN, ADJ])]
let message "Fancy word. Write `use`."
let description "Flags `leverage` as a verb and every form of `utilize`."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "We use the cache."
allows "The fund's leverage ratio must stay below four after the acquisition closes."
allows "The fund closed a leveraged buyout of the target."
allows "A longer handle gives the wrench more leverage."
allows "The leverage parameter accepts values from 1 to 125."
allows "Highly leveraged firms fail first in a downturn."
allows "Set leverage to 1 to disable margin trading."
